spark — dual-licensed
======================

spark is available under either of:

  - the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE-APACHE), OR
  - a commercial license offered by Foundation42 / Entrained.ai
    (see LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.md and contact chris@foundation42.org).

You may pick whichever fits your use case. Open-source users, students,
researchers, and most downstream projects should use Apache 2.0 — it
imposes no copyleft and grants explicit patent rights.

The commercial license is for organizations that want:

  - a path free of Apache 2.0's attribution / NOTICE-file requirements,
  - indemnification, support, or a contractual SLA,
  - use without distributing the corresponding NOTICE.

Both licenses cover the same code. There is no "open core" / "premium
features" split — the entire spark library (Element contract, layout
walker, markdown and ANSI producers, component registry, effects
substrate, rendering pipeline, shaders, and tooling) is available
under either license at the licensee's choice.

Contact
-------

Christian Beaumont — chris@foundation42.org
Foundation42 — https://foundation42.org
Entrained.ai  — https://entrained.ai

Third-party
-----------

Vendored dependencies carry their own licenses in this repository and
are NOT covered by the licenses above:

  - vendor/cmark — the CommonMark reference parser, under its own
    license (see vendor/cmark/LICENSE).
  - vendor/stb — stb_image, public domain (see the notice at the top
    of vendor/stb/stb_image.h).

Vulkan, FreeType, HarfBuzz, and glfw are linked by the HOST
executable, not vendored or distributed here — their licenses travel
with the host's link step. Fonts are loaded from the running system
and are not distributed in this repository.

The Apache 2.0 license file applies to all original source code and
documentation in this repository (`src/`, `docs/`, `shaders/`,
`examples/`, `build.zig`, `build.zig.zon`, `README.md`). It does not
extend to documents that hosts or users feed through spark at runtime
— those belong to their authors.
